    "updated_at": "2021-02-21T02:49:21Z",
    "body": "Could you post the outputs of the following two commands?\r\n\r\n```\r\nuname -m\r\nuname -s\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy guess is that this is an unexpected output in one of these two commands causing the installer to fail. If I'm right, then you should be able to override it with the following command:\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\ncurl -fsSL https://starship.rs/install.sh | bash -s -- -a x86_64\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut it's also possible that the machine architecture isn't x64 in which case I'd need to see the output of the above commands to determine what the right flags are.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
